From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Allow undefined secondary blend inputs instead of rejecting pipelines

STEAMAC-75 recurred with a complete fragment writing only color(0),
while the descriptor used OneMinusSource1Alpha. Vulkan framebuffer-dsb
allows absent secondary outputs and makes their values undefined; Metal
rejects the same pipeline. Preserve the original Index=1 location mask in
conversion results and the pipeline cache. Only where no secondary output
is declared, choose zero by replacing SRC1 factors with Zero and inverted
SRC1 factors with One. Never hide a translator loss of a real Index=1.

--- a/MoltenVKShaderConverter/MoltenVKShaderConverter/SPIRVToMSLConverter.h
+++ b/MoltenVKShaderConverter/MoltenVKShaderConverter/SPIRVToMSLConverter.h
@@ -252,6 +252,7 @@
 		SPIRVEntryPoint entryPoint;
 		bool isRasterizationDisabled = false;
 		bool isPositionInvariant = false;
+		uint32_t fragmentOutputSecondaryMask = 0;
 		bool needsOutputBuffer = false;
 		bool needsPatchOutputBuffer = false;
 		bool needsBufferSizeBuffer = false;
--- a/MoltenVKShaderConverter/MoltenVKShaderConverter/SPIRVToMSLConverter.cpp
+++ b/MoltenVKShaderConverter/MoltenVKShaderConverter/SPIRVToMSLConverter.cpp
@@ -337,6 +337,9 @@
 				}
 			}
 		}
+		// Inspect original declarations, not the emitted interface: a translator error
+		// must never turn a defined secondary output into an undefined blend value.
+		conversionResult.resultInfo.fragmentOutputSecondaryMask = pMSLCompiler->get_fragment_output_secondary_mask();
 		conversionResult.msl = pMSLCompiler->compile();
 
         if (shouldLogMSL) { logSource(conversionResult.resultLog, conversionResult.msl, "MSL", "Converted"); }
